      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I don\u0027t think you need this, since by definition the type of signal will be detectable depending on the property set i.e if pwrseq-int-gpios is set, then it is clear it is a GPIO etc.\nThe flag needs to be set in the code tables, but it doesn\u0027t have to appear in the device tree - it also begs the question about what happens if this value does not match the property that is set.\nThe idea is to check for the prop using DT_NODE_HAS_PROP and conditionally build the table entries.\nYou can be also fancy and check separately to ensure there is only one valid property using a separate loop and use a BUILD_ASSERT. Though it is likely easier to just check the size of the signal array against the number of nodes.",
